y in valhalla  leveling up grants you two skill points  which you can invest into  a pretty huge skill tree that lets you  develop your melee  ranged or stealth capabilities it seems  daunting but you can  respect your points at any point for  free so  experiment skills are mostly passive  buffs  so if you're looking for special moves  like chucking axes at dudes  head to the abilities menu abilities  aren't unlockable skills you earn by  leveling up you need to find  golden books of knowledge dotted around  the world to get them  they're usually hidden or require you to  complete some kind of puzzle to nab them  but trust me they're very worth it this  is pretty much a given  in an rpg but talk to everyone in your  settlement  especially newcomers this is how you  find new allies  spark romances and gain secret abilities  like a wolf that joins you in  battle you heard me right also fyi  people in your settlement can die so  make sure to spend time with your faves  while you can  because you never know what tragedy  might befall them  heiser  make sure to fix the barracks in your  settlement and create your own unique  yom's viking this lieutenant is sent out  to other valhalla games online and if  hired by other players  will earn you some easy money  [Music]  there are a bunch of godlike animals  scattered throughout  england i must have missed them if you  find and kill them you can have them  stuffed and put on display in your long  house  you'll need to make sure you invest in  the hunter shop back at your settlement  before you can do this  make sure to turn in your order of the  ancients medallions to the hidden one's  bureau to unlock powerful new abilities  turning in four will let you coat your  weapons and arrows in poison  which is super useful for boss fights  [Music]  there's a cute cat that hates most  people but loves sailors  if you want to find it follow oswald's  quest line and it's a random world side  event activity  that occurs towards the end